---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const contactEmail = 'contact@citizenstewardship.org';
const contactMailto = 'mailto:contact@citizenstewardship.org?subject=Citizen%20Stewardship%20privacy%20request';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="Plain-English privacy policy for Citizen Stewardship, including Cloudflare Pages hosting, Formspree contact messages, GitHub Discussions, and public submissions."
>
	<PageHero
		title="Privacy Policy"
		lede="Citizen Stewardship is a citizen-created public discussion project focused on democratic renewal and civic reform in the United States."
	/>

	<section class="section tight">
		<div class="container prose">
			<p class="privacy-note">Last updated: May 22, 2026.</p>

			<h2>Who runs this project</h2>
			<p>
				Citizen Stewardship is a citizen-created public discussion project focused on
				democratic renewal and civic reform in the United States. The public website is
				available at citizenstewardship.org and the public contact email is
				<a href={contactMailto}>{contactEmail}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>What this project collects directly</h2>
			<p>
				The site itself does not require user accounts. It does not intentionally use
				analytics or advertising trackers, sell personal information, process payments, or
				operate its own database for comments, submissions, or accounts. The site publishes
				public pages and proposal PDFs.
			</p>
			<p>
				The site does not intentionally collect sensitive personal information. Please do not
				send or post private information that does not belong in a public civic review
				process.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact form</h2>
			<p>
				The Contact page uses Formspree. If you submit the contact form, the information you
				provide, including your name, email address, subject, and message, is sent through
				Formspree and then to the site owner.
			</p>
			<p>
				The contact form is processed by Formspree. Formspree may process the information
				you submit so the message can be delivered.
			</p>

			<h2>Email</h2>
			<p>
				You may also email <a href={contactMailto}>{contactEmail}</a> directly. If you do,
				your email address and message are visible to the site owner and may be retained as
				needed to read, respond to, or keep a record of the message.
			</p>

			<h2>GitHub Discussions</h2>
			<p>
				Citizen Stewardship uses GitHub Discussions for public discussion, forum-style
				interaction, and public proposal submissions. Anything posted there is public and
				subject to GitHub's own terms and privacy policy.
			</p>

			<h2>Public submissions and comments</h2>
			<p>
				Public proposal submissions are handled through GitHub Discussions. Public
				submissions may be reviewed, discussed, linked, moved, copied, summarized, or
				referenced as part of the Citizen Stewardship public review process.
			</p>
			<p>
				Approved submissions do not mean full endorsement or final adoption. Approval means
				the submission is considered relevant enough for public review or further discussion.
			</p>

			<h2>Hosting and technical data</h2>
			<p>
				The site is hosted through Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process technical data
				such as IP address, browser information, request logs, security events, and similar
				data needed to deliver and protect the site.
			</p>
			<p>
				The site may use normal browser requests to load pages, images, proposal PDFs, CSS,
				JavaScript, fonts, and other static files needed for the website to work.
			</p>

			<h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
			<p>
				The site itself does not intentionally use analytics, advertising trackers, or its
				own tracking cookies. Browser, hosting, security, or third-party services may still
				process technical information under their own policies when you use those services or
				when they deliver required website infrastructure.
			</p>

			<h2>Third-party services</h2>
			<p>
				The site may link to third-party websites, including GitHub, Formspree, Cloudflare,
				and social platforms. Once you leave citizenstewardship.org, those services'
				policies apply.
			</p>
			<p>
				The site uses this social/Open Graph image when pages are shared:
				https://citizenstewardship.org/assets/images/citizen-stewardship-social.png.
				Social platforms may display that image and may collect data according to their own
				policies when you use or share content on those platforms.
			</p>

			<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
			<p>
				Citizen Stewardship is a public civic website and is not directed to children. Do not
				use the contact form or GitHub Discussions to submit personal information from a
				child.
			</p>

			<h2>Do not submit private or sensitive information</h2>
			<p>
				Do not post or send private personal information, doxxing material, sensitive
				personal data, confidential documents, private addresses, private phone numbers,
				passwords, medical information, financial information, or anything you do not want
				public.
			</p>

			<h2>How to request removal or correction</h2>
			<p>
				To ask for a correction or removal related to this website, email
				<a href={contactMailto}>{contactEmail}</a>. Requests involving content posted on
				GitHub Discussions may also need to be handled through GitHub, because those posts
				are hosted by GitHub and tied to GitHub accounts.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				This policy may be updated when the site changes, when public submission processes
				change, or when third-party services used by the site change. The updated date above
				will be revised when that happens.
			</p>
			<p>
				Rules for using the site, participating in discussions, and submitting ideas are
				covered in the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For privacy questions, corrections, or removal requests, email
				<a href={contactMailto}>{contactEmail}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
